+# CODEX-OPUS-C-NAMES-PLAN-20261024-A): the families of generated names whose index stands for a binding of the source --
+# a method's formals and inputs (l2_p, with l2_pr and l2_fv derived from them), its own fields (l2_q, with its
+# derived _from and _dirty, and l2_wv) and its slots (l2_s) -- keep their prefix and index, which alone make the name
+# unique, and add `_` and the binding's name when it is an ordinary identifier of C's set (l2_ident_word); a derived
+# name's tail comes after it: `l2_p0_0_var`, `l2_q0_log_from`. A binding of another spelling, an exact identifier, adds
+# nothing: the decision is its source spelling's (none binds today, l2_bind_admit). The name is appended to t, of any
+# length; only the index is formatted in a buffer, whose size two ints' digits bound. b < 0: one index. 0, or 1.
+fn: l2_tx_cname (@: L2Tx t; const: @(char prefix); int: a; int: b; const: @(LmP0Text name); const: @(char tail)) int
+    []: char num 48
+    if: t = 0 || prefix = 0 || tail = 0
+        return: 1
+    if: b < 0 && c.snprintf(num, 48U, "%d", a) < 0
+        return: 1
+    if: b >= 0 && c.snprintf(num, 48U, "%d_%d", a, b) < 0
+        return: 1
